\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The reference failure landscape. Instability (best-worst Dice gap) vs.\ catastrophic failure rate across four segmenters on MoNuSAC. Each point is a query. The structural anti-correlation---low-instability queries tend toward catastrophic failure, high-instability queries tend away from it---is a universal property of the two-stage pipeline, explained by the entropy of the matching map (Section~\ref {sec:theory}).}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:anticorrelation}{{1}{2}{The reference failure landscape. Instability (best-worst Dice gap) vs.\ catastrophic failure rate across four segmenters on MoNuSAC. Each point is a query. The structural anti-correlation---low-instability queries tend toward catastrophic failure, high-instability queries tend away from it---is a universal property of the two-stage pipeline, explained by the entropy of the matching map (Section~\ref {sec:theory})}{figure.1}{}}
