\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Empirical verification of the entropy-failure relationship. (a) Instability vs.\ matching map entropy. (b) CFR vs.\ matching map entropy. The anti-correlation is confirmed ($r=-0.491$, $p<0.001$), but the CFR relationship is non-monotonic: the mid-entropy regime is the most dangerous, refining the theoretical prediction of Theorem~1.}}{7}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:entropy_bins}{{4}{7}{Empirical verification of the entropy-failure relationship. (a) Instability vs.\ matching map entropy. (b) CFR vs.\ matching map entropy. The anti-correlation is confirmed ($r=-0.491$, $p<0.001$), but the CFR relationship is non-monotonic: the mid-entropy regime is the most dangerous, refining the theoretical prediction of Theorem~1}{figure.4}{}}
